<title>USA: Vermont Lieutenant Gov backs off from tax hike.</title>
<headline>Vermont Lieutenant Gov backs off from tax hike.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Victorious in his race for Vermont lieutenant governor, Democrat Doug Racine has stopped talking about raising income taxes.</p>
<p>Racine said he no longer believes that broad-based tax hikes will be needed to pay for property tax reform. The lieutenant governor explained that a faster growing economy would create new state tax revenues without raising taxes.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
